[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene is captured from a 3/4 overhead angle (40 degrees) to showcase the volume and texture of two white ceramic plates resting on an aged oak table. Each plate features a generous base of fluffy, light brown whole wheat couscous, with a delicate, opaque white cod fillet placed alongside a vibrant, colorful heap of roasted diced zucchini, halved cherry tomatoes, and halved Kalamata olives. The cod is perfectly cooked, showing tender, flaky white layers with a light sheen from a squeeze of lemon juice. The diced zucchini cubes are tender with slight caramelization and charred edges from the oven. The cherry tomatoes are softened, their juices mingling slightly with the olive oil and couscous. A fresh, bright yellow lemon wedge sits at the edge of each plate. Shallow depth of field keeps the front plate in crisp focus while the second plate behind is softly blurred. Soft natural light from a window to the left creates gentle, realistic shadows. Props include a stainless steel fork resting on the linen cloth and a few stray grains of couscous and a single kalamata olive half on the wood surface. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a lived-in, warm, authentic home kitchen. Includes subtle imperfections: a tiny sauce drip on the rim, slightly uneven browning, and a natural crumb trail. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no hands, no faces, no text."
]
